1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,600
Inflation is down. So why does your grocery bill still look like this?

2
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:14,000
Lower inflation doesn't usually mean lower prices. It means prices are rising more slowly.

3
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:28,000
Imagine the same basket costs one hundred. Ten percent inflation takes it to one hundred and ten. Then inflation drops to two percent. The basket now costs one hundred and twelve point two.

4
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:35,600
Think of a car slowing down. It's still moving forward. It hasn't gone into reverse.

5
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:44,400
So a lower inflation rate can still leave you paying more for exactly the same things.

6
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:55,000
That's why your receipt can feel so different from the headline that says…
